{"name":"Cyber Grunge","title":"Cyber Grunge","revision":236676,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Cyber_Grunge","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Cyber Grunge is an aesthetic that blends elements of Grunge, streetwear, and Y2K Futurism, sometimes with slight military influences. This style, which has been observed since approximately 2022, is characterized by bold silhouettes, utilitarian features, and an infusion of futuristic elements. It largely utilizes \"subversive basics,\" referring to simple clothing with alternative or avant-garde details such as cut-outs, mesh, and pockets. The influence of the Y2K revival is also prevalent, with accessories, prints, and silhouettes from that era being common."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Cyber Grunge seamlessly blends elements of rebellion, urban edge, and a touch of Y2K nostalgia. The fashion style borrows from the concept of \"subversive basics\" and the preference for the earthy, muted color palette often associated with Grunge, including browns, greens, and greys. An utilization of layered androgynous clothing with a mix of oversized and distressed items are characteristic for Cyber Grunge. Wearing large headphones, goggles, or other futuristic accessories enhance the overall look."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Tops, Bottoms, and Dresses"},{"kind":"list","text":"Crop tops (most commonly tank tops)"},{"kind":"list","text":"T-shirt"},{"kind":"list","text":"Maxi and mini skirt"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cargo pants"},{"kind":"list","text":"Track pants"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Footwear"},{"kind":"list","text":"El Dantes Boots"},{"kind":"list","text":"New Rock Boots"},{"kind":"list","text":"Gordon Jack Platforms"},{"kind":"list","text":"Swear Alternative"},{"kind":"list","text":"Destroy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shelley's"},{"kind":"list","text":"Demonia"},{"kind":"list","text":"Buffalo"},{"kind":"list","text":"The ART Company"},{"kind":"list","text":"El Naturalista"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sella"},{"kind":"list","text":"Madfish"},{"kind":"list","text":"Roxy"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Accessories"},{"kind":"list","text":"Necklaces akin to Fairy Grunge (pearl, handmade, etc.)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Stockings"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Hats"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bucket hat"},{"kind":"list","text":"Baseball cap"},{"kind":"list","text":"Knit beanie"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Outer Garments"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cardigan"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cropped jackets"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Textures, Materials and Miscellaneous"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mesh and sheer clothing"},{"kind":"list","text":"Layering"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jeans"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Film"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Matrix series (1999-2021)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Anime & Manga"},{"kind":"list","text":"Serial Experiments Lain (1998)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ghost in the Shell (1995)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Resources"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Blogs"},{"kind":"list","text":"Apricotcat"},{"kind":"list","text":"Despar Zine"}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/1/10/Cfg_military.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20231213013449","caption":"Cfg military","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Cfg_military.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0247-1.webp","localAvailable":true},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/5/51/Stargirl.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20220804132433","caption":"Cyber Grunge · Visual reference 02","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Stargirl.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0247-2.webp","localAvailable":true}]}